{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "28841660-e1db-8ae5-bd93-96b3ccb94b1e",
  "created_at": "2026-02-24T18:12:17-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Sarah Mensah",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Denise Arruda",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:09:41-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works storm line, this is Denise."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:09:44-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, good evening. I am calling about the storm drain. I know City Hall is closed now, it is after six, but I was told this number is for the storm problems."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:09:55-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's right, you've got the right place. Which drain is it?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:09:59-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is on the corner near my building, three sixty-six Annandale Road. The drain is full to the top, the water just sits, it is not draining at all. [pause] Hello? Did you hear me?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:10:11-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I did, three sixty-six Annandale Road. Sorry, go ahead, I think we're talking over each other a little."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:10:17-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there is a delay on this line, I am sorry. It has been like this since the nor'easter, last weekend, Saturday into Sunday. Two days now and the water is still standing there. Cars are driving through and it splashes on the sidewalk."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:10:31-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. Is the water coming toward any buildings, or is it staying in the street?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:10:37-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "For now it stays in the street, but it is very close to the curb. And I must say, it was not this bad last winter. Last winter the water went down after the storm, always. Now nothing. Somebody should have cleaned this already."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:10:51-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I hear you. Could be leaves or slush packed down in the grate, or something further down the line. Either way a crew needs to look at it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:01-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, so will you open a work order? I want to know this. And for what date? [crosstalk]"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:07-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm opening one now, go ahead, I'm sorry, you were saying?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:11-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I am asking for what date the work is. Not only that you write it down. Every time somebody says they write it down and then nothing happens."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:21-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. The order goes in tonight, dated today, the twenty-fourth. Crews are still catching up from the storm, so I'd expect somebody out there in the next few days, and they work the drains in order of how bad they are. Yours being fully blocked helps."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:36-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "A few days. Hmm. That is long, but all right. Do you need a number to call me back?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:43-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes please, in case the supervisor wants to confirm the date with you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:48-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It is four zero one, five five five, zero one seven three. And my name is Sarah Mensah."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:11:54-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Got it. Sarah Mensah, four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-seven-three, three sixty-six Annandale Road, storm drain on the corner, full and not draining. Did I get that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:12:03-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, that is correct. Thank you. I hope this time somebody comes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:12:08-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I've flagged it as a full blockage. Take care, Ms. Mensah, and stay off that corner if you can."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-24T18:12:15-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. Good night."
    }
  ],
